Key Implementation Details
Authentication Flow:
User enters phone number (10-digit Indian)
Firebase sends OTP
User verifies OTP
Firebase returns ID token
Send token to /auth/login/ or /auth/register/*
Backend returns JWT access + refresh tokens
Store tokens in localStorage
Attach Bearer token to all API requests
Auto-refresh on 401 using refresh token
Multi-Language Implementation:
Three languages: English (en), Hindi (hi), Telugu (te)
Use i18next with complete translations
### Multi-Language Implementation:

**Static Translations (i18n):**
- For all UI elements: labels, buttons, messages, menu items
- Pre-defined in JSON files: `en.json`, `hi.json`, `te.json`
- Use `t('key')` function from `useTranslation` hook
- Complete translations for all three languages

**Dynamic Translations (Free API):**
- For chatbot responses, user-generated content, API responses
- Uses MyMemory API (primary) - 5000 words/day free, no key needed
- Uses Lingva API (fallback) - Google Translate proxy, no key needed
- Translation caching to reduce API calls
- Use `<TranslatedText>` component or `translateDynamic()` function

**Language Switching:**
- User changes language in settings
- Instantly updates all UI (static translations)
- Dynamically translates cached content
- Persists to localStorage and backend
- Updates document font family based on language

Update document.body.setAttribute('data-lang', lng) for font switching
All text must come from translation files, no hardcoded strings
